From 1ba8c48b01787538dcc0c2894354809d541aa152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali Asiri <assiri@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 08:11:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i18n(desktop): bring the Arabic locale back to full coverage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`ar.ts` has been drifting since the locale landed in 5b6990e7a. Because
`defineLocale()` merges overrides on top of `en`, a key that is missing from a
locale silently renders in English and `tsc` cannot catch it — so the gap grew
quietly as new UI shipped.

Measured against this commit's `en.ts`: `ar.ts` supplied 2335 of 3113 keys, so
783 strings rendered in English (74.8% coverage). At the time Arabic landed the
gap was 413 keys; the 370 added since are new UI, not regressions — no string
that was ever translated has reverted.

This restores 100% coverage. Four sections were absent entirely (`billingBlock`,
`findInPage`, `starmap`, `webhooks`); the rest were partial, with `settings`
accounting for 323 of the missing keys, then `skills` (74), `webhooks` (60),
`commandCenter` (52) and `shell` (45).

Notes for review:

- Purely additive. No previously translated string is altered — the 11 deleted
  lines in the diff are existing entries that gained a trailing comma because a
  new sibling was inserted after them.
- Terminology follows what the locale already shipped (الإعدادات، المزوّد،
  البوابة، الجلسة، المهارات …), mined from the existing entries rather than
  chosen afresh.
- Arrow-function entries keep their exact parameter lists, type annotations and
  `${...}` placeholders; plural branches follow the existing
  `count === 1 ? … : …` style used elsewhere in the file.
- `settings.fieldLabels` / `settings.fieldDescriptions` entries are emitted as
  flat dotted keys, matching the existing style — these override the records
  that `defineFieldCopy()` has already flattened.
- Product names and protocol identifiers (Nous, MCP, SSH, Webhooks, GitHub,
  Hermes Cloud) are left in Latin script, as elsewhere in the file.

Verified: 100% key parity with `en.ts`; no pre-existing entry changed; prettier
clean under the repo config; `tsc` reports no new diagnostic categories and zero
syntax errors. The desktop i18n tests cover the locale registry rather than
catalogue contents, so they are unaffected by this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
